{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CBn1FwPX41Ze6VQpcWRWRC","type":"tool_result","content":"# Claude Code CLI Commands and Flags Summary\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `claude` | Start interactive session |\n| `claude \"query\"` | Start interactive session with initial prompt |\n| `claude -p \"query\"` | Query via SDK, then exit (non-interactive) |\n| `claude -c` | Continue most recent conversation in current directory |\n| `claude -r \"<session>\"` | Resume session by ID or name |\n| `claude update` | Update to latest version |\n| `claude auth login/logout/status` | Authentication management |\n| `claude agents` | Monitor and dispatch parallel background sessions |\n\n## Critical Flags\n\n### `-p` / `--print`\n**Print response without interactive mode** (exit after completion)\n- Used for scripting and programmatic usage\n- Example: `claude -p \"explain this function\"`\n- Can pipe content: `cat file | claude -p \"query\"`\n- Enables non-interactive SDK usage\n- Works with flags like `--output-format`, `--json-schema`, `--max-budget-usd`\n\n### `-c` / `--continue`\n**Load the most recent conversation in current directory**\n- Skips background sessions, SDK sessions, and `/loop` sessions\n- `claude -p --continue` includes those skipped sessions\n- Includes sessions that added this directory with `/add-dir`\n- Example: `claude -c` or `claude -c -p \"Check for type errors\"`\n\n### `-r` / `--resume`\n**Resume a specific session by ID or name**\n- Shows interactive picker if no session specified\n- Searches by ID across current project and git worktrees, then all projects\n- Example: `claude -r \"auth-refactor\" \"Finish this PR\"`\n- Background sessions appear marked with `bg` in picker\n- Name-based search included\n\n### `-n` / `--name`\n**Set a display name for the session**\n- Shown in `/resume` and terminal title\n- Resume named sessions with `claude --resume <name>`\n- Automatically applies variants if name already exists\n\n## Other Essential Flags\n\n- `--bg` / `--background` - Start as background agent, return immediately\n- `--model` - Set model (sonnet, opus, haiku, fable, or full name)\n- `--effort` - Set effort level (low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultracode)\n- `--permission-mode` - Begin in specified permission mode (default, plan, auto, bypassPermissions, etc.)\n- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` - Skip permission prompts\n- `--output-format` - Specify output (text, json, stream-json)\n- `--input-format` - Specify input format (text, stream-json)\n- `--settings` - Override settings for session\n- `--add-dir` - Add additional working directories"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[REDACTED]","uuid":"[REDACTED]","timestamp":"2026-08-27T12:59:24.313Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":106543,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Claude Code CLI Commands and Flags Summary\n\n## Key Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `claude` | Start interactive session |\n| `claude \"query\"` | Start interactive session with initial prompt |\n| `claude -p \"query\"` | Query via SDK, then exit (non-interactive) |\n| `claude -c` | Continue most recent conversation in current directory |\n| `claude -r \"<session>\"` | Resume session by ID or name |\n| `claude update` | Update to latest version |\n| `claude auth login/logout/status` | Authentication management |\n| `claude agents` | Monitor and dispatch parallel background sessions |\n\n## Critical Flags\n\n### `-p` / `--print`\n**Print response without interactive mode** (exit after completion)\n- Used for scripting and programmatic usage\n- Example: `claude -p \"explain this function\"`\n- Can pipe content: `cat file | claude -p \"query\"`\n- Enables non-interactive SDK usage\n- Works with flags like `--output-format`, `--json-schema`, `--max-budget-usd`\n\n### `-c` / `--continue`\n**Load the most recent conversation in current directory**\n- Skips background sessions, SDK sessions